  "description": "It never fails; the best sets of trails are usually a hike, and more times than not, that hike usually involves some hills. Enter our 1.8. This is the Dr. Jekyll to our 1.3's Mr. Hide. Able to handle anything its single-speed brother can, the 1.8 with its 8-speed rear cassette gets you up and over those rollers without killing you in the process. And just like our 1.3, with its Six-Shooter convertible dropouts, you can convert this into a single-speed bike in no time flat. No more having to choose between a single speed and a geared bike; with the 1.8 you can have them both.\nFull 4130 chromoly frame w/ internal head tube, Euro BB shell, removable cable guides, and our \"Six-Shooter\" interchangeable dropout system\nAvailable in two sizes: Short (21.8\" TT) and Long (22.3\" TT)\nX Fusion Velvet R 80mm travel suspension fork with X-15 tool-less 15mm thru axle\nTruvativ Ruktion 1.0 crank with The Hive E*Thirteen LS1 chain guide system\nSyncros FR38 OS double-butted alloy riser bar and FR50 V2 OS alloy stem\n6000 series alloy CNC'd Thin Pedal w/removable pins and sealed bearings\nAlienation Skylark double-wall rims\nTektro Draco hydraulic rear brake with 160mm wave rotor\nPivotal seat and post\nRitchey Logic Zero Comp internal headset\nSRAM X-4 rear derailleur with 11/32 8-speed chrome plated rear cog",
